On Mon, Jun 01, 2015 at 02:09:03PM +0800, kbuild test robot wrote:
> tree:   git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/dgc/linux-xfs xfs-sparse-inode
> head:   22ce1e1472fda6ce740cee966bb8e25a3cc662bd
> commit: 09b566041344fcfa9ae3c1b010f364137173894a [17/18] xfs: skip unallocated regions of inode chunks in xfs_ifree_cluster()
> config: i386-randconfig-a1-0601 (attached as .config)
> reproduce:
>   git checkout 09b566041344fcfa9ae3c1b010f364137173894a
>   # save the attached .config to linux build tree
>   make ARCH=i386 
> 
> All error/warnings:
> 
>    fs/built-in.o: In function `xfs_ifree_cluster':
> >> xfs_inode.c:(.text+0x17ac84): undefined reference to `__umoddi3'
> 

Looks like this is due to the ASSERT() added to the sparse cluster case
in the loop. Since this is just verifying the inode offset, I suspect a
simple cast should fix it. E.g., the following fixes the 32-bit compile
with the config below for me:

        if ((xic->alloc & XFS_INOBT_MASK(inum - xic->first_ino)) == 0) {
                 ASSERT(((int)(inum - xic->first_ino) %
                         inodes_per_cluster) == 0);
                 continue;
         }

I'll send along a patch for this as well.

Brian

